## 🔧 공통 Validation 인터페이스

### Validator 인터페이스
```java
@FunctionalInterface
public interface Validator<T> {
    
    ValidationResult<T> validate(T input);
    
    /**
     * 여러 Validator를 조합하여 모든 검증 실행 (모든 오류 수집)
     */
    static <T> Validator<T> combine(Validator<T>... validators) {
        return input -> {
            List<String> errors = new ArrayList<>();
            
            for (Validator<T> validator : validators) {
                ValidationResult<T> result = validator.validate(input);
                if (result.isFailure()) {
                    errors.addAll(result.getErrors());
                }
            }
            
            return errors.isEmpty() 
                ? ValidationResult.success(input)
                : ValidationResult.failure(errors);
        };
    }
    
    /**
     * 여러 Validator를 체인으로 연결 (첫 번째 실패에서 중단)
     */
    static <T> Validator<T> chain(Validator<T>... validators) {
        return input -> {
            for (Validator<T> validator : validators) {
                ValidationResult<T> result = validator.validate(input);
                if (result.isFailure()) {
                    return result;
                }
            }
            return ValidationResult.success(input);
        };
    }
}
```

### ValidationResult 클래스
```java
public sealed interface ValidationResult<T> {
    
    boolean isSuccess();
    boolean isFailure();
    T getValue();
    List<String> getErrors();
    <R> ValidationResult<R> map(Function<T, R> mapper);
    
    static <T> ValidationResult<T> success(T value) {
        return new Success<>(value);
    }
    
    static <T> ValidationResult<T> failure(String error) {
        return new Failure<>(List.of(error));
    }
    
    static <T> ValidationResult<T> failure(List<String> errors) {
        return new Failure<>(errors);
    }
    
    record Success<T>(T value) implements ValidationResult<T> {
        @Override
        public boolean isSuccess() { return true; }
        
        @Override
        public boolean isFailure() { return false; }
        
        @Override
        public T getValue() { return value; }
        
        @Override
        public List<String> getErrors() { return List.of(); }
        
        @Override
        public <R> ValidationResult<R> map(Function<T, R> mapper) {
            return success(mapper.apply(value));
        }
    }
    
    record Failure<T>(List<String> errors) implements ValidationResult<T> {
        @Override
        public boolean isSuccess() { return false; }
        
        @Override
        public boolean isFailure() { return true; }
        
        @Override
        public T getValue() { 
            throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot get value from failure result");
        }
        
        @Override
        public List<String> getErrors() { return errors; }
        
        @Override
        public <R> ValidationResult<R> map(Function<T, R> mapper) {
            return new Failure<>(errors);
        }
    }
}
```

## 🧪 테스트 패턴

### Validator 단위 테스트
```java
@Test
@DisplayName("이메일 검증 - 성공")
void emailValidator_shouldPassWithValidEmail() {
    // Given
    TestCommand command = new TestCommand("test@example.com");
    
    // When
    ValidationResult<TestCommand> result = EmailValidator.validate().validate(command);
    
    // Then
    assertThat(result.isSuccess()).isTrue();
    assertThat(result.getValue()).isEqualTo(command);
}

@Test
@DisplayName("이메일 검증 - 실패 (잘못된 형식)")
void emailValidator_shouldFailWithInvalidFormat() {
    // Given
    TestCommand command = new TestCommand("invalid-email");
    
    // When
    ValidationResult<TestCommand> result = EmailValidator.validate().validate(command);
    
    // Then
    assertThat(result.isFailure()).isTrue();
    assertThat(result.getErrors()).contains("validation.email.invalid");
}
```

